        ("p", r"<b>Example 1: $f(x) = x^2$.</b> Step 1: $f(x + h) = (x + h)^2 = x^2 + 2xh + h^2$. Step 2: $f(x + h) - f(x) = 2xh + h^2 = h(2x + h)$. Step 3: $\frac{h(2x + h)}{h} = 2x + h$. Step 4: $\lim_{h \to 0}(2x + h) = 2x$. So $(x^2)' = 2x$."),
        ("p", r"<b>Example 2: $f(x) = \sin x$.</b> By the difference-of-sines formula, $\sin(x + h) - \sin x = 2\cos\!\big(x + \tfrac{h}{2}\big)\sin\tfrac{h}{2}$. Divide by $h$:"),
        ("eq", r"\frac{\sin(x + h) - \sin x}{h} = \cos\!\Big(x + \frac{h}{2}\Big)\cdot\frac{\sin(h/2)}{h/2} \;\xrightarrow[h \to 0]{}\; \cos x \cdot 1 = \cos x"),
